  "content": "[Intro 1]\n\n[Intro 2]\n\n[Intro 3]\n\n[Intro 4]\n\n[Intro 5]\n[Amaj7/E]\n[B/E]\n[Amaj7/E]\n[B/E]\n[Amaj7/E]\n[B/E]\n[Amaj7/E]\n[B/E]\n[Amaj7/E]\n[B/E]\n[Amaj7/E]\n[B/E]\n[Amaj7/E]\n[B/E]\n[E]\n\n[Verse 1]\n[A/E]Watcher of the skies\n[E]Watcher of all\n[E7sus4]His is a world alone no\n[E]world is his own\n[A/E]He whom life can no\n[E]longer surprise\n[E7sus4]Raising his eyes beholds a\n[Emaj7]planet unknown\n\n[Verse 2]\n[Amaj7/E]\n[B/E]\n[Amaj7/E]\n[B/E]\n[Amaj7/E]Creatures shaped this\n[B/E]planet's soil\n[Amaj7/E]Now thier regin has come to an end\n[B/E]Has\n[Amaj7/E]life again destroyed life\n[B/E]Do they play elsewhere, do they know\n[Amaj7/E]more than their [G#m]childhood\n[F#sus4]games? [F#][G#]\n\n[Verse 3]\n[A/E]Maybe the lizard's\n[E]shed it's tail This\n[E7sus4]is the end of man's long\n[E]union with Earth\n\n[Intrelude]\n[Am6]\n[Gm6]\n[Fm6]\n[C/G]\n[G#]  [C#/G#]  [E/G#]\n[A]  [D/A]  [F/A]\n[A#]  [D#/A#]  [F#/A#]\n[B]  [E/B]  [A]  [E/G#]\n\n[Chorus]\n[A/E]Judge not this race by\n[E]empty remains\n[E7sus4]Do you judge God by his creatuers\n[E]when they are dead?\n[A/E]For now, the lizard's\n[E]shed it's tail\n[E7sus4]This is the end of man's long\n[E]union with Earth\n\n[Verse 4]\n[Amaj7/E]\n[B/E]For\n[Amaj7/E]life alone to\n[B/E]life as one\n[Amaj7/E]Think not now your journey's done\n[B/E]For\n[Amaj7/E]though your ship be sturdy, no\n[B/E]Mercy has the sea, Will you sur-\n[Amaj7/E]vive on the [G#m]ocean of\n[F#sus4]being? [F#][G#]\n\n[Verse 5]\n[A/E]Come ancient children\n[E]hear what I say\n[E7sus4]This is my par ting council for\n[E]you on your way\n\n[Intrelude]\n[Am6]\n[Gm6]\n[Fm6]\n[C/G]\n[G#]  [C#/G#]  [E/G#]\n[A]  [D/A]  [F/A]\n[A#]  [D#/A#]  [F#/A#]\n[B]  [E/B]  [A]  [E/G#]\n\n[Chorus]\n[A/E]Sadly now your thoughts\n[E]turn to the stars\n[E7sus4]Where we have gone you know you\n[E]never can go.\n[A/E]Whatcher of the skies\n[E]whatcher of all\n[E7sus4]This is your fate alone, this\n[E]fate is your own.\n\n[Bridge 1]\n[E5]\n[C#dim]\n[E5]\n[C#dim]\n[Em7]\n[Em6]\n[Em7]\n[E5]\n\n[Bridge 2]\n[F#m]\n\n[Outro]\n[F#m]  [E]\n[E]  [F#m]\n[A]  [G]\n[G]  [F#m]\n[C#dim7]  [B/F#]\n[Dmaj7]\n[C#m7]\n[Bm7]\n[F#]",
